	"nodes":[
		{"id":"53c820ade6014ee1","type":"text","text":"|                                                               |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Some SQLs used in DQ validation are incorrect – needs review. |\n| Duplicate cards appearing in the catalog – needs fix.         |\n| Meta naming — clarify details with Pavan.                     |\n|                                                               |\n","x":-228,"y":-158,"width":528,"height":138},
		{"id":"e2203239cc740a83","type":"text","text":"## **09 Dec 2025 — Issues & Action Points**\n\n### **🔴 Priority: DQ**\n\n1. Some SQLs used in DQ validation are incorrect — needs review.\n2. Good rules are being marked as **“Action Required”** incorrectly.\n3. Some rules that have **passed** are still showing **low scores** — scoring logic needs verification.\n\n---\n\n### **Development**\n\n1. Duplicate cards appearing in the catalog — needs fix.\n2. Notification pop-ups behaving unexpectedly.\n3. Filters not working as expected.\n4. Meta naming — clarify details with Pavan.\n5. Failed-record WebSocket not functioning.\n6. Execution failed status — behaviour inconsistent, needs verification.\n7. Industry-standard state mapping not aligned — review required.\n8. Dev ↔ UAT relationship mapping missing in UI.\n\n### **UI/UX & Display**\n\n1. Remove “Total Rules Count” statement from conversation view.\n2. Remove rule name from UI.\n3. “Overall Status” should be displayed as **Results**.\n4. Table view formatting must be consistent across screens.\n\n### **UAT**\n\n1. Data Quality — when modified, validation status is not showing.  \n      \n    All environments : Check how to invoke cluster as soon log in happens to UI   \n      \n    Everyone please mark this as issues to be fixed , also remeber that we are seeing some changes in UI and conversation   \n    with upstream environments and not in dev and uat   \n      \n    Nissy Elsa John above are points listed by me at my best please let me know if I have missed anything , Thank you","x":-1320,"y":-200,"width":340,"height":573},
		{"id":"319ac39d21506a35","type":"text","text":"\n| rule id                  | overall status      | be_sql query                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   | result_sql_query                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          | error                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        | responsible team | comment                                                                 |\n| ------------------------ | ------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ---------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| 69382147051270538987e118 | verification failed | SELECT COUNT(1) AS invalid_records FROM dev_vena.dec9_e2e_testing.sample_tb_export_cleansed_sheet1 tb JOIN dev_vena.dec9_e2e_testing.sample_gl_export_cleansed_sheet tr ON tb.last_month = tr.amount WHERE tb.last_month IS NOT NULL AND tr.amount IS NOT NULL AND (SELECT SUM(tb.last_month) FROM dev_vena.dec9_e2e_testing.sample_tb_export_cleansed_sheet1 tb) <> (SELECT SUM(tr.amount) FROM dev_vena.dec9_e2e_testing.sample_gl_export_cleansed_sheet tr) | SELECT * FROM (SELECT *, COUNT(*) OVER (PARTITION BY tb.last_month) AS cnt FROM dev_vena.dec9_e2e_testing.sample_tb_export_cleansed_sheet1 tb JOIN dev_vena.dec9_e2e_testing.sample_tb_export_cleansed_sheet1 tr ON tb.last_month = tr.last_month WHERE tb.last_month IS NOT NULL AND tr.last_month IS NOT NULL) sub WHERE cnt > 1                                                        | [TABLE_OR_VIEW_NOT_FOUND] The table or view `dev_vena`.`dec9_e2e_testing`.`sample_gl_export_cleansed_sheet` cannot be found. Verify the spelling and correctness of the schema and catalog.<br>If you did not qualify the name with a schema, verify the current_schema() output, or qualify the name with the correct schema and catalog.<br>To tolerate the error on drop use DROP VIEW IF EXISTS or DROP TABLE IF EXISTS. SQLSTATE: 42P01; line 1 pos 107 | meta             | while generating sql query, table name is incorrect for table named gl. |\n| 69382137051270538987e116 | execution failed    | SELECT COUNT(1) AS invalid_records FROM (SELECT trx.*, coa.*, COUNT(*) OVER (PARTITION BY trx.account_number) AS cnt FROM dev_vena.dec9_e2e_testing.sample_gl_export_cleansed_sheet1 trx LEFT JOIN dev_vena.dec9_e2e_testing.sample_tb_export_cleansed_sheet1 coa ON LTRIM(RTRIM(trx.account_number)) = LTRIM(RTRIM(coa.account_number)) WHERE trx.account_number IS NOT NULL) sub WHERE coa.account_number IS NULL                                            | SELECT * FROM (SELECT trx.*, coa.*, COUNT(*) OVER (PARTITION BY trx.account_number) AS cnt FROM dev_vena.dec9_e2e_testing.sample_gl_export_cleansed_sheet1 trx LEFT JOIN dev_vena.dec9_e2e_testing.sample_tb_export_cleansed_sheet1 coa ON LTRIM(RTRIM(trx.account_number)) = LTRIM(RTRIM(coa.account_number)) WHERE trx.account_number IS NOT NULL) sub WHERE coa.account_number IS NULL |                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              |                  |                                                                         |\n| 69382136051270538987e115 | execution failed    | SELECT COUNT(1) AS invalid_records FROM (SELECT tb.*, gl.account_number FROM dev_vena.dec9_e2e_testing.sample_tb_export_cleansed_sheet1 tb LEFT JOIN dev_vena.dec9_e2e_testing.sample_gl_export_cleansed_sheet1 gl ON tb.account_number = gl.account_number) sub WHERE account_number IS NULL                                                                                                                                                                  | SELECT * FROM (SELECT tb.*, gl.account_number FROM dev_vena.dec9_e2e_testing.sample_tb_export_cleansed_sheet1 tb LEFT JOIN dev_vena.dec9_e2e_testing.sample_gl_export_cleansed_sheet1 gl ON tb.account_number = gl.account_number) sub WHERE account_number IS NULL                                                                                                                       |                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              |                  |                                                                         |\n| 69382123051270538987e113 | verification failed | SELECT COUNT(1) AS invalid_records FROM dev_vena.dec9_e2e_testing.sample_gl_export_cleansed_sheet1 WHERE date NOT BETWEEN @start_date AND @end_date                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            | SELECT * FROM dev_vena.dec9_e2e_testing.sample_gl_export_cleansed_sheet1 WHERE date NOT BETWEEN '2023-01-01' AND '2023-12-31'                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             | <br>[PARSE_SYNTAX_ERROR] Syntax error at or near '@'. SQLSTATE: 42601 (line 1, pos 122)<br><br>== SQL ==<br>SELECT COUNT(1) AS invalid_records FROM dev_vena.dec9_e2e_testing.sample_gl_export_cleansed_sheet1 WHERE date NOT BETWEEN @start_date AND @end_date<br>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------^^^<br>                                                         |                  | it is syntax error where it could not understand @ special character.   |\n| 69382105051270538987e10f | verification failed | SELECT COUNT(1) AS invalid_records FROM dev_vena.dec9_e2e_testing.sample_tb_export_cleansed_sheet1 GROUP BY _Account_Number, _Subsidiary_ID, _Department HAVING ABS(SUM(COALESCE(last_month, 0.0))) > 0.01                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     | SELECT * FROM (SELECT *, COUNT(*) OVER (PARTITION BY account_number, _Subsidiary_ID, _Department) AS cnt FROM dev_vena.dec9_e2e_testing.sample_tb_export_cleansed_sheet1) sub WHERE cnt > 1                                                                                                                                                                                               | [UNRESOLVED_COLUMN.WITH_SUGGESTION] A column, variable, or function parameter with name `_Account_Number` cannot be resolved. Did you mean one of the following? [`account_number`, `_2_months_ago`, `_3_months_ago`, `event_id`, `formula_numeric`]. SQLSTATE: 42703; line 1 pos 108                                                                                                                                                                        |                  | change in the name for column                                           |\n| 