		{"id":"c8befaef6c675af9","type":"text","text":"1. **Chart of Accounts (CoA) – ChartOfAccounts\\n\\n**\n\t1. 1.1 Rule Definition: **All critical fields in Chart of Accounts must be present and populated**\\n\\nRule Specification: ChartOfAccounts._dim, ChartOfAccounts._member_name, ChartOfAccounts._parent_name, ChartOfAccounts._operator must be populated\\n\\nQuery Expression: SELECT *\\nFROM ChartOfAccounts coa\\nWHERE coa._dim IS NULL OR LTRIM(RTRIM(coa._dim)) = ''\\n   OR coa._member_name IS NULL OR LTRIM(RTRIM(coa._member_name)) = ''\\n   OR coa._parent_name IS NULL OR LTRIM(RTRIM(coa._parent_name)) = ''\\n   OR coa._operator IS NULL OR LTRIM(RTRIM(coa._operator)) = '';\\n\\n\n\t2. 1.2 Rule Definition: **Accounts must be unique in Chart of Accounts**\\n\\nRule Specification: ChartOfAccounts._member_name must be unique\\n\\nQuery Expression:\\nSELECT\\n    coa._member_name,\\n    COUNT(*) AS cnt\\nFROM ChartOfAccounts coa\\nWHERE coa._member_name IS NOT NULL\\nGROUP BY coa._member_name\\nHAVING COUNT(*) > 1;\\n\\n \n\t3. 1.3 Rule Definition: **Parent accounts' hierarchy integrity must be maintained in Chart of Accounts**\\n\\nRule Specification: Every value in ChartOfAccounts._parent_name must also have a record where that value is in ChartOfAccounts._member_name\\n\\nQuery Expression: SELECT *\\nFROM ChartOfAccounts child\\nLEFT JOIN ChartOfAccounts parent\\n    ON child._parent_name = parent._member_name\\nWHERE child._parent_name IS NOT NULL\\n  AND parent._member_name IS NULL;\\n\\n\n\t4. 1.4 Rule Definition: **No self-parenting of members in Chart of Accounts**\\n\\nRule Specification: ChartOfAccounts._member_name must be different from ChartOfAccounts._parent_name\\n\\nQuery Expression: SELECT *\\nFROM ChartOfAccounts\\nWHERE _member_name = _parent_name;\\n\\n\n\t5. 1.5 Rule Definition: **Operator values in Chart of Accounts must be valid**\\n\\nRule Specification: ChartOfAccounts._operator values must be + or -\\n\\nQuery Expression: SELECT *\\nFROM ChartOfAccounts\\nWHERE _operator NOT IN ('+', '-');\\n\\n\n\t6. 1.6 Rule Definition: **No special characters in any of the fields in Chart of Accounts**\\n\\nRule Specification: Columns in ChartOfAccounts should not contain any special characters, and should only contain alphanumerics or underscore.\\n\\nQuery Expression:\\nSELECT *\\nFROM ChartOfAccounts\\nWHERE PATINDEX('%[^A-Za-z0-9 _]%', CAST(_dim AS NVARCHAR(4000))) > 0\\n   OR PATINDEX('%[^A-Za-z0-9 _]%', CAST(_member_name AS NVARCHAR(4000))) > 0\\n   OR PATINDEX('%[^A-Za-z0-9 _]%', CAST(_member_alias AS NVARCHAR(4000))) > 0\\n   OR PATINDEX('%[^A-Za-z0-9 _]%', CAST(_parent_name AS NVARCHAR(4000))) > 0\\n   OR PATINDEX('%[^A-Za-z0-9 _]%', CAST(_operator AS NVARCHAR(4000))) > 0\\n   OR PATINDEX('%[^A-Za-z0-9 _]%', CAST(_cmd AS NVARCHAR(4000))) > 0\\n   OR PATINDEX('%[^A-Za-z0-9 _]%', CAST(_member_id AS NVARCHAR(4000))) > 0\\n   OR PATINDEX('%[^A-Za-z0-9 _]%', CAST(_external_id AS NVARCHAR(4000))) > 0;\\n\\n\n2. **Trial Balance – TrialBalance\\n\\n**\n\t1. 2.1 Rule Definition: Account Number in Trial Balance must be populated\\n\\nRule Specification: TrialBalance._Account_Number must be populated\\n\\nQuery Expression:\\nSELECT *\\nFROM TrialBalance tb\\nWHERE tb.[_Account Number] IS NULL\\n   OR LTRIM(RTRIM(tb.[_Account Number])) = '';\\n\\n\n\t2. 2.2 Rule Definition: Subsidiary ID in Trial Balance must be populated\\n\\nRule Specification: TrialBalance._Subsidiary_ID must be populated\\n\\nQuery Expression:\\nSELECT *\\nFROM TrialBalance tb\\nWHERE tb.[_Subsidiary ID] IS NULL\\n   OR LTRIM(RTRIM(tb.[_Subsidiary ID])) = '';\\n\\n\n\t3. 2.3 Rule Definition: For a given Trial Balance extract, each Account–Subsidiary pair should appear at most once with a specific period.\\n\\nRule Specification: The combination TrialBalance._Account_Number + TrialBalance._Subsidiary_ID must be unique within a specific period\\n\\nQuery Expression:\\nSELECT\\n    tb.[_Account Number],\\n    tb.[_Subsidiary ID],\\n    COUNT(*) AS cnt\\nFROM TrialBalance tb\\nGROUP BY tb.[_Account Number], tb.[_Subsidiary ID], tb._Period\\nHAVING COUNT(*) > 1;\\n\\n\n\t4. 2.4 Rule Definition: Trial balance amounts must balance out to a zero by account, subsidiary and department for the reporting period\\n\\nRule Specification: For all records in TrialBalance, grouped by TrialBalance._Subsidiary_ID, ABS(SUM(TrialBalance._Last_Month)) must be equal to 0.\\n\\nQuery Expression:\\nSELECT\\n    tb.[_Account Number],\\n    tb.[_Subsidiary ID],\\n    tb.[_Department],\\n    SUM(COALESCE(tb.[_Last Month], 0.0)) AS last_month_total\\nFROM TrialBalance tb\\nGROUP BY\\n    tb.[_Account Number],\\n    tb.[_Subsidiary ID],\\n    tb.[_Department]\\nHAVING ABS(SUM(COALESCE(tb.[_Last Month], 0.0))) > 0.01; -- adjust tolerance\\n\\n\n3. **Transactions – Transactions\\n\\n**\n\t1. 3.1Rule Definition: Required fields populated\\n(e.g., _Account Number, _Amount, _Date, _Document Number)\\n\\nSELECT *\\nFROM Transactions trx\\nWHERE trx.[_Account Number] IS NULL\\n      OR LTRIM(RTRIM(trx.[_Account Number])) = ''\\n   OR trx._Amount IS NULL\\n   OR trx._Date IS NULL\\n   OR trx.[_Document Number] IS NULL\\n      OR LTRIM(RTRIM(trx.[_Document Number])) = '';\\n\\n\n\t2. 3.2 Rule Definition: Transactions must balance by account, document and period\\n\\nRule Specification: For all records in Transactions, grouped by Transactions._Account_Number, Transactions._Subsidiary, and Transactions._Period, ABS(SUM(Transactions._Amount)) must be 0.\\n\\nQuery Expression:\\nSELECT\\n    trx.[_Account Number],\\n    trx.[_Document_Number],\\n    trx.[_Period],\\n    SUM(trx._Amount) AS total_amount\\nFROM Transactions trx\\nGROUP BY\\n    trx.[_Account Number],\\n    trx.[_Document_Number],\\n    trx.[_Period]\\nHAVING ABS(SUM(trx._Amount)) > 0.01; -- adjust tolerance\\n\\n\n\t3. 3.3 Rule Definition: Unique line keys must be unique\\n\\nRule Specification: Transactions._Line_Unique_Key must be unique\\n\\nQuery Expression:\\nSELECT\\n    trx.[_Line Unique Key],\\n    COUNT(*) AS cnt\\nFROM Transactions trx\\nWHERE trx.[_Line Unique Key] IS NOT NULL\\nGROUP BY trx.[_Line Unique Key]\\nHAVING COUNT(*) > 1;\\n\\n\n\t4. 3.4 Rule Definition: All transactions must be within the reporting window.\\n\\nRule Specification: All Transactions._Date must be between YYYY-MM-01 and YYYY-MM-31\\n\\nQuery Expression:\\nSELECT *\\nFROM Transactions trx\\nWHERE trx._Date NOT BETWEEN @start_date AND @end_date;\\n\\n\n\t5. 3.5 Rule Definition: For foreign transactions, the amount must be calculated as foreign currency amount multiplied by the exchange rate.\\n\\nRule Specification: Transactions._Amount must be equal to Transactions._Amount (Foreign Currency) * Transactions._Exchange Rate\\n\\nQuery Expression:\\nSELECT *\\nFROM Transactions trx\\nWHERE trx.[_Amount (Foreign Currency)] IS NOT NULL\\n  AND trx.[_Exchange Rate] IS NOT NULL\\n  AND trx._Amount IS NOT NULL\\n  AND ABS(trx._Amount - (trx.[_Amount (Foreign Currency)] * trx.[_Exchange Rate])) > 0.01;\\n\\n\n4. **Cross-File Reconciliation\\n\\n**\n\t1. 4.1 Rule Definition: Accounts used in Transactions must be present in CoA. That is, no orphan account numbers in transaction data.\\n\\nRule Specification: Transactions._Account_Number must exist in ChartOfAccounts._member_name\\n\\nQuery Expression:\\nSELECT DISTINCT\\n    trx.[_Account Number]\\nFROM Transactions trx\\nLEFT JOIN ChartOfAccounts coa\\n    ON LTRIM(RTRIM(trx.[_Account Number])) = LTRIM(RTRIM(coa._member_name))\\nWHERE trx.[_Account Number] IS NOT NULL\\n  AND coa._member_name IS NULL;\\n\\n\n\t2. 4.2 Rule Definition: Accounts used in Trial Balance must be present in CoA. That is, no orphan account numbers in Trial Balance data.\\n\\nRule Specification: TrialBalance._Account_Number must exist in ChartOfAccounts._member_name\\n\\nQuery Expression:\\nSELECT DISTINCT\\n    tb.[_Account Number]\\nFROM TrialBalance tb\\nLEFT JOIN ChartOfAccounts coa\\n    ON tb.[_Account Number] = coa._member_name\\nWHERE tb.[_Account Number] IS NOT NULL\\n  AND coa._member_name IS NULL;\\n\\n\n\t3. 4.3 Rule definition: The total balance in the Trial Balance for last month must match the total activity coming from the Transactions for that same period, across all accounts and subsidiaries. If difference ≠ ~0, your overall ledger doesn't tie out.\\n\\nRule specification: SUM(TrialBalance._Last_Month) must be equal to SUM(Transactions._Amount) for all records where Transactions._Period = <Last_Month_Period> and TrialBalance._Account_Number = Transactions._Account_Number and TrialBalance._Subsidiary = Transactions._Subsidiary.\\n\\nQuery expression:\\nSELECT\\n    SUM(tb.[_Last Month]) AS tb_last_month_total,\\n    SUM(COALESCE(tlm.trx_last_month, 0)) AS trx_last_month_total,\\n    SUM(tb.[_Last Month])\\n      - SUM(COALESCE(tlm.trx_last_month,0)) AS difference\\nFROM TrialBalance tb\\nLEFT JOIN (\\n    SELECT\\n        trx.[_Account Number],\\n        trx.[_Subsidiary],\\n        SUM(trx._Amount) AS trx_last_month\\n    FROM Transactions trx\\n    WHERE trx._Period = @period\\n    GROUP BY\\n        trx.[_Account Number],\\n        trx.[_Subsidiary]\\n) tlm\\n    ON tb.[_Account Number] = tlm.[_Account Number]\\n   AND tb.[_Subsidiary] = tlm.[_Subsidiary];\n \n ","x":-5080,"y":-660,"width":1120,"height":2180},
