		{"id":"cffd0d83a00fe978","x":-8020,"y":-4700,"width":720,"height":2320,"type":"text","text":"CONTEXT: FP&A_DQ_RULE_HIERARCHY_ROLLUP_INTEGRITY  \n  \nBUSINESS_INTENT  \nEnsure financial balances roll up correctly across the FP&A account hierarchy.  \nEach parent account’s balance must equal the signed aggregation of all its descendant accounts.  \n  \nFP&A_CONCEPTS (LOGICAL, NOT PHYSICAL)  \nAccount  \n- Account_Code        : business account identifier  \n- Parent_Account_Code : immediate parent in hierarchy  \n- Rollup_Operator     : indicates contribution to parent ('ADD' | 'SUBTRACT')  \n  \nBalance  \n- Account_Code        : account identifier  \n- Org_Unit            : company / subsidiary / cost center  \n- Period              : reporting period  \n- Balance_Amount      : financial amount for the period  \n  \nRULE_LOGIC  \n1. Identify top-level (root) accounts with no parent.  \n2. Recursively traverse the Account hierarchy to collect all descendants.  \n3. Propagate rollup sign using Rollup_Operator:  \n   ADD → +1, SUBTRACT → -1 (cumulative through levels).  \n4. Attach Balance_Amount to each descendant account.  \n5. Aggregate signed balances per Parent Account and Org_Unit.  \n6. Compare aggregated value with the Parent Account’s reported balance.  \n7. Flag mismatches beyond tolerance.  \n  \nFAILURE_INDICATES  \n- Broken or incomplete account hierarchy  \n- Incorrect rollup operator configuration  \n- Missing leaf-level balances  \n- Balances posted at incorrect hierarchy level  \n- Financial statement misstatement risk  \n  \nTOLERANCE  \nAbsolute difference > configurable threshold (e.g., 0.01)  \n  \nSQL_INTENT_TEMPLATE (LOGICAL)  \n  \nWITH RECURSIVE AccountHierarchy AS (  \n  -- Root accounts  \n  SELECT  \n    Account_Code        AS Root_Account,  \n    Account_Code        AS Current_Account,  \n    CASE  \n      WHEN Rollup_Operator = 'ADD' THEN 1  \n      WHEN Rollup_Operator = 'SUBTRACT' THEN -1  \n      ELSE 0  \n    END AS Rollup_Factor  \n  FROM Account  \n  WHERE Parent_Account_Code IS NULL  \n  \n  UNION ALL  \n  \n  -- Descendant accounts  \n  SELECT  \n    h.Root_Account,  \n    a.Account_Code,  \n    h.Rollup_Factor *  \n      CASE  \n        WHEN a.Rollup_Operator = 'ADD' THEN 1  \n        WHEN a.Rollup_Operator = 'SUBTRACT' THEN -1  \n        ELSE 0  \n      END  \n  FROM AccountHierarchy h  \n  JOIN Account a  \n    ON a.Parent_Account_Code = h.Current_Account  \n),  \n  \nComputedRollup AS (  \n  SELECT  \n    h.Root_Account,  \n    b.Org_Unit,  \n    SUM(COALESCE(b.Balance_Amount, 0) * h.Rollup_Factor) AS Computed_Balance  \n  FROM AccountHierarchy h  \n  LEFT JOIN Balance b  \n    ON b.Account_Code = h.Current_Account  \n  GROUP BY  \n    h.Root_Account,  \n    b.Org_Unit  \n)  \n  \nSELECT  \n  c.Root_Account            AS Parent_Account,  \n  c.Org_Unit,  \n  c.Computed_Balance,  \n  b.Balance_Amount          AS Reported_Parent_Balance,  \n  c.Computed_Balance - b.Balance_Amount AS Difference  \nFROM ComputedRollup c  \nJOIN Balance b  \n  ON b.Account_Code = c.Root_Account  \nAND b.Org_Unit = c.Org_Unit  \nWHERE ABS(c.Computed_Balance - b.Balance_Amount) > Threshold;"},
		{"id":"c28bbc8c829b17cd","x":-7783,"y":-5327,"width":843,"height":487,"type":"text","text":"1. search dq context. \n2. get tables\n3. get columns\n4. get knowledge context\n5. verify\n6. execute"},
		{"id":"9a60790336986779","x":-9140,"y":-5261,"width":1260,"height":461,"type":"text","text":"SELECT COUNT(1) AS invalid_records FROM dev_vena.dec15_testing_348.coa_hierarchy_format_in c JOIN (SELECT h.Root_Account, b.Org_Unit, SUM(COALESCE(b.Balance_Amount, 0) * h.Rollup_Factor) AS Computed_Balance FROM (SELECT Account_Code AS Root_Account, Account_Code AS Current_Account, CASE WHEN Rollup_Operator = 'ADD' THEN 1 WHEN Rollup_Operator = 'SUBTRACT' THEN -1 ELSE 0 END AS Rollup_Factor FROM dec15_testing_348.coa_hierarchy_format_in WHERE Parent_Account_Code IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT h.Root_Account, a.Account_Code, h.Rollup_Factor * CASE WHEN a.Rollup_Operator = 'ADD' THEN 1 WHEN a.Rollup_Operator = 'SUBTRACT' THEN -1 ELSE 0 END FROM AccountHierarchy h JOIN dec15_testing_348.coa_hierarchy_format_in a ON a.Parent_Account_Code = h.Current_Account) AS AccountHierarchy LEFT JOIN dec15_testing_348.sample_gl_export_cleansed_sheet1 b ON b.account_number = h.Current_Account GROUP BY h.Root_Account, b.Org_Unit) AS ComputedRollup ON c.account_number = ComputedRollup.Root_Account AND c.Org_Unit = ComputedRollup.Org_Unit WHERE ABS(ComputedRollup.Computed_Balance - c.Balance_Amount) > 0.01;"},
		{"id":"f3cb065570cf7ab1","x":-2958,"y":-1920,"width":758,"height":860,"type":"text","text":"  \nFP&A_CONCEPTS (LOGICAL, NOT PHYSICAL)  \nAccount  \n- Account_Code        : business account identifier  \n- Parent_Account_Code : immediate parent in hierarchy  \n- Rollup_Operator     : indicates contribution to parent ('ADD' | 'SUBTRACT')  \n  \nBalance  \n- Account_Code        : account identifier  \n- Org_Unit            : company / subsidiary / cost center  \n- Period              : reporting period  \n- Balance_Amount      : financial amount for the period  \n  \nRULE_LOGIC  \n1. Identify top-level (root) accounts with no parent.  \n2. Recursively traverse the Account hierarchy to collect all descendants.  \n3. Propagate rollup sign using Rollup_Operator:  \n   ADD → +1, SUBTRACT → -1 (cumulative through levels).  \n4. Attach Balance_Amount to each descendant account.  \n5. Aggregate signed balances per Parent Account and Org_Unit.  \n6. Compare aggregated value with the Parent Account’s reported balance.  \n7. Flag mismatches beyond tolerance.  \n  \nFAILURE_INDICATES  \n- Broken or incomplete account hierarchy  \n- Incorrect rollup operator configuration  \n- Missing leaf-level balances  \n- Balances posted at incorrect hierarchy level  \n- Financial statement misstatement risk  \n  \nTOLERANCE  \nAbsolute difference > configurable threshold (e.g., 0.01)  \n  \nSQL_INTENT_TEMPLATE (LOGICAL)  \n  \nWITH RECURSIVE AccountHierarchy AS (  \n  -- Root accounts  \n  SELECT  \n    Account_Code        AS Root_Account,  \n    Account_Code        AS Current_Account,  \n    CASE  \n      WHEN Rollup_Operator = 'ADD' THEN 1  \n      WHEN Rollup_Operator = 'SUBTRACT' THEN -1  \n      ELSE 0  \n    END AS Rollup_Factor  \n  FROM Account  \n  WHERE Parent_Account_Code IS NULL  \n  \n  UNION ALL  \n  \n  -- Descendant accounts  \n  SELECT  \n    h.Root_Account,  \n    a.Account_Code,  \n    h.Rollup_Factor *  \n      CASE  \n        WHEN a.Rollup_Operator = 'ADD' THEN 1  \n        WHEN a.Rollup_Operator = 'SUBTRACT' THEN -1  \n        ELSE 0  \n      END  \n  FROM AccountHierarchy h  \n  JOIN Account a  \n    ON a.Parent_Account_Code = h.Current_Account  \n),  \n  \nComputedRollup AS (  \n  SELECT  \n    h.Root_Account,  \n    b.Org_Unit,  \n    SUM(COALESCE(b.Balance_Amount, 0) * h.Rollup_Factor) AS Computed_Balance  \n  FROM AccountHierarchy h  \n  LEFT JOIN Balance b  \n    ON b.Account_Code = h.Current_Account  \n  GROUP BY  \n    h.Root_Account,  \n    b.Org_Unit  \n)  \n  \nSELECT  \n  c.Root_Account            AS Parent_Account,  \n  c.Org_Unit,  \n  c.Computed_Balance,  \n  b.Balance_Amount          AS Reported_Parent_Balance,  \n  c.Computed_Balance - b.Balance_Amount AS Difference  \nFROM ComputedRollup c  \nJOIN Balance b  \n  ON b.Account_Code = c.Root_Account  \nAND b.Org_Unit = c.Org_Unit  \nWHERE ABS(c.Computed_Balance - b.Balance_Amount) > Threshold;"},
		{"id":"ce1f696c60bbe2ec","x":-2120,"y":-1920,"width":760,"height":960,"type":"text","text":"**Entities**\n\n**Financial Account**  \n- Account Type  \n- Account Name  \n- Reporting Hierarchy  \n\n**Trial Balance**  \n- Reporting Period  \n- Entity  \n- Total Debits  \n\n**General Ledger**  \n- Transaction Date  \n- Source Document  \n- Currency  \n\n**Financial Statement**  \n- Statement Type  \n- Reporting Period  \n- Entity  \n\n**KPIs**  \n- KPI Name  \n- Target Value  \n- Actual Value  \n\n**Relationships**  \nFinancial Account —classifies→ Trial Balance  \nTrial Balance —validates→ General Ledger  \nGeneral Ledger —feeds→ Financial Statement  \nFinancial Statement —informs→ KPIs  \n\n**Hierarchies**  \nAccount Hierarchy: Financial Account → Sub-Account  \nReporting Hierarchy: Entity → Department  \n\n**Business Concepts / Events**  \nBudgeting Cycle: The process of allocating financial resources for future periods.  \nVariance Analysis: The examination of differences between planned and actual financial performance.  \n\n**Conceptual Interaction Flow**  \nFinancial Accounts classify transactions in the General Ledger, which validates data integrity through the Trial Balance. Accurate Trial Balances enable the generation of reliable Financial Statements. These statements inform KPIs, guiding management decisions and future budgeting cycles. Variance Analysis assesses performance against these budgets, ensuring alignment with financial goals."},
		{"id":"72256be6328e759e","x":-3960,"y":-1840,"width":820,"height":400,"type":"text","text":"WITH RECURSIVE AccountHierarchy AS (SELECT Account_Code AS Root_Account, Account_Code AS Current_Account, CASE WHEN Rollup_Operator = 'ADD' THEN 1 WHEN Rollup_Operator = 'SUBTRACT' THEN -1 ELSE 0 END AS Rollup_Factor FROM dec11_e2e_test_sharepoint_v13.coa_hierarchy_format_in WHERE Parent_Account_Code IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT h.Root_Account, a.Account_Code, h.Rollup_Factor * CASE WHEN a.Rollup_Operator = 'ADD' THEN 1 WHEN a.Rollup_Operator = 'SUBTRACT' THEN -1 ELSE 0 END FROM AccountHierarchy h JOIN dec11_e2e_test_sharepoint_v13.coa_hierarchy_format_in a ON a.Parent_Account_Code = h.Current_Account), ComputedRollup AS (SELECT h.Root_Account, b.Org_Unit, SUM(COALESCE(b.Balance_Amount, 0) * h.Rollup_Factor) AS Computed_Balance FROM AccountHierarchy h LEFT JOIN dec11_e2e_test_sharepoint_v13.sample_tb_export_cleansed_sheet1 b ON b.account_number = h.Current_Account GROUP BY h.Root_Account, b.Org_Unit) SELECT c.Root_Account AS Parent_Account, c.Org_Unit, c.Computed_Balance, b.Balance_Amount AS Reported_Parent_Balance, c.Computed_Balance - b.Balance_Amount AS Difference FROM ComputedRollup c JOIN dec11_e2e_test_sharepoint_v13.sample_tb_export_cleansed_sheet1 b ON b.account_number = c.Root_Account AND b.Org_Unit = c.Org_Unit WHERE ABS(c.Computed_Balance - b.Balance_Amount) > Threshold;"}
